       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US.\n- A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of about 1,000 mg. Doses this high raise the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm it. I can enter it with a note that you verified the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
